% M1-T23. A refutation that has to branch, over numbers near the compile-time cap.
%
% 2A(x1 + x2 + x3) = 5A with A = 2^53 = 9007199254740992, i.e. test_matrix.ml's
% lin_le/parity-branching multiplied through. It is UNSAT by parity -- 2(x1+x2+x3) = 5
% has no integer solution -- and parity is exactly what bounds reasoning cannot see, so
% the root fixpoint settles without refuting anything and the search has to branch and
% close both children at every level. That makes this the model where the biggest legal
% numbers meet the trace machinery: every slack, every Combine divisor and every .opb
% constant in the emitted proof is seventeen digits wide, and the refutation still has
% to verify.
%
% The row's magnitude -- |rhs| + sum |coeff| * max(|lo|, |hi|) -- is 207165582859042816,
% 71.9% of Checked.limit. near_limit_ne_sat.fzn is the satisfiable companion and drives
% the disequality's worse envelope path; this one drives the search.
array [1..3] of int: c = [18014398509481984, 18014398509481984, 18014398509481984];
var 0..3: x1 :: output_var;
var 0..3: x2 :: output_var;
var 0..3: x3 :: output_var;
constraint int_lin_eq(c, [x1, x2, x3], 45035996273704960);
solve satisfy;
